From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] efi/sb: prefer legacy SHIM_LOCK verify so pre-SBAT kernels
 boot under shim >= 15

ONIE supports platforms that still build older (pre-6.x) Linux kernels.
Those kernels' EFI stub predates SBAT and carries no .sbat section.

grub 2.14 verifies the images it loads (including the kernel) using shim's
newer image-loader protocol when shim provides it (shim >= 15/16).  That
path makes an .sbat section MANDATORY, so shim rejects a pre-SBAT kernel
("No .sbat section data" -> grub "bad shim loader signature") even though
the kernel's Authenticode signature is valid.

shim also still installs the legacy SHIM_LOCK verify protocol, which
enforces the signature but treats SBAT as optional for images verified
through the protocol (shim's verify_sbat_section() returns success on a
missing .sbat when in_protocol).  Prefer that protocol when it is present
so a validly-signed old kernel boots.  shim and grub keep full SBAT
enforcement in the boot chain up to grub itself; only the kernel is then
verified by signature alone -- which is how ONIE (signing its own kernels)
verified kernels before the shim/grub modernization.

Signed-off-by: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
---
 grub-core/kern/efi/sb.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/grub-core/kern/efi/sb.c
+++ b/grub-core/kern/efi/sb.c
@@ -236,6 +236,20 @@
   shim_loader = grub_efi_locate_protocol (&shim_loader_guid, 0);
   shim_lock = grub_efi_locate_protocol (&shim_lock_guid, 0);
 
+  /*
+   * ONIE: when the legacy SHIM_LOCK verify protocol is available, prefer it
+   * over shim's newer image-loader protocol.  shim's load_image path makes an
+   * .sbat section MANDATORY in every image it loads, which rejects ONIE's
+   * older (pre-6.x) kernels whose EFI stub predates SBAT -- "No .sbat section
+   * data" -> "bad shim loader signature" -- even though the kernel signature
+   * is valid.  The SHIM_LOCK->verify path still enforces the signature but
+   * treats SBAT as optional (in_protocol), so a validly-signed old kernel
+   * boots.  shim and grub keep full SBAT enforcement in the boot chain up to
+   * grub itself; only the kernel is verified by signature alone.
+   */
+  if (shim_lock != NULL)
+    shim_loader = NULL;
+
   /* shim is missing, check if GRUB image is built with --disable-shim-lock. */
   if (shim_loader == NULL && shim_lock == NULL)
     {
